      "problem": "Which of the following shows the point $C(4,-2)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $C.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $C$ has an $x$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units to the *right*, in the positive direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $C$ has a $y$-coordinate of $-2,$ so we move $2$ units *down*, in the negative direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14199677/assets/68f55dd9851c7fa3805dec284aad2a9eb7e07b77a94a3f6b4b9b8ddcfd630baf.png)",
